    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0345" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1194.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-05T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 30, 7 p.m.</p>
                <p>Department requested Navy May 2nd to instruct Commander of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Petrel</hi> to request the opening of customhouse,
                    Puerto Plata, and continuance <pb facs="0346" n="230" xml:id="pg230"/> of proper
                    collection of customs. He has further been instructed to advise this Department
                    should this request not be complied with, and to inform it of what action will
                    be necessary to bring compliance by authorities. He will see that all American
                    and foreign interests are given proper protection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
